  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "u0hfYtrj1kmcZFNamNwgQHytycA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:38.525Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Wigo4it is the ICT cooperative for the social services of the four largest Dutch cities. Like Dimpact it is a federated buyer: one relationship covers the systems of all four members, and the decision is taken jointly rather than city by city.\n\nWhat differentiates it from the other cooperative is the domain. The research notes that social services work is document-heavy, which gives it direct relevance to intelligent document processing \u2014 the evidence a case rests on arrives as documents, and the decisions taken on those documents are the substance of the service.\n\nThe two properties reinforce each other. A document-heavy domain generates the kind of decisions a record layer exists for, taken about individuals and open to challenge afterwards, while the federated structure means one integration serves four large municipalities. Its recorded tooling \u2014 Common Ground, and participation in the GZAC proof of concept \u2014 places it in the same technical family as the other Dutch leads here, so the integration surface is shared rather than bespoke.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**1 \u00b7 parallel track**\n- Wigo4it (NL)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> ICT cooperative for the social services of the four largest Dutch cities. \u2014 Second federated buyer. The social domain is document-heavy, so direct IDP relevance.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:32:38.525335Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:32:38.525339Z"
    }
  },
